No nodes specified to start. Starting all nodes configured in '/home/ubuntu/.simulaqron/simulaqron_network.json'.
Network with name default is seems to be already running.
This is based on the fact that the PID file '/home/ubuntu/.simulaqron_pids/simulaqron_network_default.pid' already exists.

To try to stop the running backend, run 'simulaqron stop --name default'.
If the error persist, you might need to use 'simulaqron reset' commands to reset the
backend execution state:
* 'simulaqron reset pidfiles' will delete *all* the PID files in '/home/ubuntu/.simulaqron_pids'.
* 'simulaqron reset processes' will *kill all* running simulaqron-related processes.

Check the help of the simulaqron reset command ('simulaqron reset -h') to know more.
